@startuml
title Detonate Bomb Remotely

hide footbox

legend top right
  |<#E6E6E6> View (React / TypeScript) |
  |<#CFE3F7> Controller (Java) |
  |<#D8F0D8> Model (Java) |
endlegend
autonumber

skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor LightCyan
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor DarkSlateGray
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor White
skinparam ActorBorderColor DarkSlateGray
skinparam ArrowColor SlateGray
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor SlateGray
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor DarkSlateGray
skinparam DefaultFontName Arial
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor LightYellow
    BorderColor Orange
}


' ==========================================
' Participants, coloured by MVC layer as in "Explode Bomb" (see legend).
' Part of the player's step of stage.update(), after "Place Bomb".
' Always includes "Explode Bomb".
' ==========================================
actor "Player" as user
actor "Time" as time

participant "GameLoop" as view #E6E6E6

participant "GameBridge" as bridge #CFE3F7

participant "game : Game" as game #D8F0D8
participant "stage : Stage" as stage #D8F0D8
participant "player : Player" as player #D8F0D8

user -> view : press detonate key
view -> view : inputMask |= DETONATE (cleared on release)
time -> view : next animation frame
view -> bridge : tick(inputMask)
bridge -> game : update(input)
game -> stage : update(input)

note over stage, player
  Runs within one tick, in the player's step of stage.update(),
  after "Place Bomb". input.detonatePressed() is true only in the
  tick the key goes down, as for the bomb key: one press sets off
  one bomb.
end note

opt player alive and input.detonatePressed()
    stage -> player : hasDetonator()
    player --> stage : detonator

    opt detonator
        stage -> stage : oldest = first bomb in bombs\nthat is not yet queued
        note right of stage
          bombs keeps placement order ("Place Bomb").
          Bombs placed before the Detonator was picked
          up still count; they keep their fuse too.
        end note

        opt oldest exists
            stage -> stage : explosionQueue.add(oldest)
            ref over stage, player
              Explode Bomb: the bomb explodes in this same
              tick, in the bombs step of stage.update().
            end ref
        end
    end
end

note over stage, player
  Nothing happens without the Detonator, without bombs,
  or while the player is dead. The Detonator is lost on
  death, and the stage's bombs go with the old stage.
end note

stage --> game
game --> bridge
bridge --> view
note over view, bridge : The frame is then drawn as in\n"Explode Bomb" (getState, draw, sounds).

@enduml
